The user wants a JavaScript code that removes the "(age X)" pattern from a string, where X can be any number. This is a regex replacement task.

The pattern to match would be:
- Opening parenthesis: `\(age`
- Space
- One or more digits: `\d+`
- Closing parenthesis: `\)`

So the regex would be: `/\(age \d+\)/`

