# JavaScript Code to Remove "(age X)" Pattern

Here are several ways to accomplish this:

## **Method 1: Using `replace()` with Regex**

```javascript
const text = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
const cleaned = text.replace(/\(age \d+\)/g, '');

console.log(cleaned);
// Output: "july 7 1994  London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## **Method 2: Remove Extra Spaces**

```javascript
const text = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
const cleaned = text.replace(/\(age \d+\)\s*/g, '').trim();

console.log(cleaned);
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## **Method 3: Reusable Function**

```javascript
function removeAgePattern(text) {
  return text.replace(/\(age \d+\)\s*/g, '').trim();
}

// Test with different ages
console.log(removeAgePattern("july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK"));
console.log(removeAgePattern("july 7 1994 (age 25) London, UK"));
console.log(removeAgePattern("july 7 1994 (age 100) London, UK"));

// All output: "july 7 1994 London, UK"
```

## **Regex Explanation**

| Pattern | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| `\(age` | Matches literal "(age" |
| ` ` | Matches a space |
| `\d+` | Matches one or more digits (any age) |
| `\)` | Matches literal ")" |
| `\s*` | Matches optional whitespace after |
| `g` | Global flag (removes all occurrences) |

## **Complete Example with Multiple Cases**

```javascript
const examples = [
  "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)",
  "july 7 1994 (age 25) London, UK",
  "july 7 1994 (age 100) London, UK (1994-07-07)",
  "Multiple (age 5) and (age 10) ages"
];

examples.forEach(text => {
  const cleaned = text.replace(/\(age \d+\)\s*/g, '').trim();
  console.log(`Original: ${text}`);
  console.log(`Cleaned:  ${cleaned}\n`);
});
```

**Method 2 or 3 is recommended** as it also removes the extra space left after removing the age pattern! 😊

